<title>ARGENTINA: ARGENTINE BANCO RIO BOND PROGRAM EXPANSION OKAYED.</title>
<headline>ARGENTINE BANCO RIO BOND PROGRAM EXPANSION OKAYED.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Argentine Bolsa Monday said it had authorized local Banco Rio, controlled by Spain's Banco Santander, to extend a global bond issue program from $600 million to up to $900 million.</p>
<p>Rio was also authorized to list two previously announced mid-term fifth and six bond series in dollars -- part of the same program -- for $500 million and $80 million respectively, the Buenos Aires Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>((Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
